<mjml>
<!--
  IMPECCABLE DIRECTION CONTRACT
  THESIS: the distributor's circular mark sits to the left, with the
  invitation headline wrapping around it — the same read as an author photo
  beside a byline headline — so identity and invitation land as one visual
  unit instead of a small icon and a separate paragraph. Sized as a supporting
  identity mark (60px), not a hero image — the user's reference mockup used a
  larger circle only to demonstrate the wrap position, not the target size.
  OWN-WORLD: apps/portal/DESIGN.md, inherited exactly — Deep Navy #0B1D3A /
  Cobalt Blue #1565FF (single CTA only) / Slate Blue #5B6B7F / Pale Stone
  #F2F4F7 / Light Blue Grey #E6ECF2, Inter, hard 0px corners everywhere
  except identity circles. Amber (#F2864D, tints amber-light/amber-border)
  now backs the benefits list as a callout — DESIGN.md's own documented use
  ("Amber... personality... tints back status badges and callouts"), not a
  second competing action color. The Stocdup logo asset is navy-on-white by
  design — never recolored or placed on a dark band.
  Revision history on this template: v1 recolored the Stocdup logo white on
  a navy band (wrong — the real asset is navy-on-white, never inverted). v2
  moved to a small inline byline icon (safer for email clients, but read as
  disconnected from the headline). v3 (this version) matches the layout of
  the user's reference mockup (screenshots/email_layout.png), at a smaller
  size per their follow-up (the mockup's circle was to show wrap/position,
  not target size): a circular mark, floated left, with the headline text
  wrapping around it directly — built
  with a real CSS float on the image inside one mj-text block (the simplest,
  most broadly-supported float case: one image, one paragraph, not a
  multi-column layout), with an explicit clearfix so later content doesn't
  collide if the headline text is shorter than the image.
  STORY: a customer sees the supplier's mark and the invitation as one
  connected unit, reads what they'll be able to do, and acts.
  FIRST VIEWPORT: white card — Stocdup logo, then the distributor's circular
  mark with a Title-weight (16px/600, not a big display headline) sentence
  wrapping beside it, an Amber-backed callout for the benefits list, a
  single Cobalt CTA. Consistent 24px (xl token) rhythm between every block,
  32px card edges — no ad hoc padding values.
  FORM: extends an established world onto a new (email) surface — no
  concept-seed tournament run; the visual system and copy were already
  fully specified going in (root conversation, not this file).
  FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with
  the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md.

  IMPECCABLE CRITIQUE PASS (dual-agent, apps/api/src/mail/templates/invite.mjml):
  found the "consistent 24px rhythm" claim above was not actually enforced —
  every un-styled mj-text silently inherited MJML's own default padding
  (10px top, 25px sides) on top of each section's declared padding, adding
  hidden top/side offsets. Fixed via a global `mj-text` padding:0 default in
  mj-attributes, so section padding is now the ONLY spacing source. Also
  fixed: body copy now matches DESIGN.md's `body` token exactly (14px/400/
  1.5, was an invented 15px/1.6); the 13px contact-line text (not on
  DESIGN.md's scale at all) and the 12px expiry/footer text (right size,
  missing the Label token's 500-weight/0.02em tracking) now both fully
  adopt the `label` token; bullets got a true hanging indent (wrapped lines
  were falling back to the left margin instead of aligning under the text);
  the circular logo's border-radius was off by 1px for a true circle once
  its own border is included; the floated logo now shrinks on narrow
  viewports (a mobile-only `mj-style` rule) since the wrap was reported to
  go to 5 cramped lines otherwise; the "Your account will be connected to…"
  line now uses Slate Blue (an actual DESIGN.md token, not an invented
  color) to differentiate it from the headline, per a cognitive-load
  finding that headline and body were too visually similar. The reviewed
  broken-Stocdup-logo finding was traced to an empty `src` and initially
  looked like a real defect — root-caused to the ad hoc preview script used
  to generate review screenshots, not this template or the real send
  pipeline (which always supplies a real, non-empty URL; confirmed via a
  real send through the actual production pipeline).

  LOGO CORRECTION (post-critique): the header used the full wordmark image
  (stocdup-logo.png) baked as a single asset. Wrong — this codebase never
  does that for UI chrome; every real usage (apps/admin's Sidebar and login
  page, apps/portal's equivalents) pairs the icon-only mark
  (stocdup-logo-only.png) with live text, "stocd" in Deep Navy + "up" in
  Cobalt Blue. Now matches the Sidebar's own compact chrome-header sizing
  (36px icon, 18px/700 text, 10px gap) rather than the bigger 34px/700
  Display-token treatment used on full-page login heroes — this header is
  chrome, not a hero moment.

  V4 — LAYOUT REBASE (screenshots/email_layout2.png): the user supplied a
  second reference mockup with a different composition, not just a
  different skin, and asked for the layout only — DESIGN.md's real tokens
  stayed in force, not the mockup's rounded card, drop shadow, or blue
  checkmarks.
  - The identity mark, headline, detail copy, and CTA now live together
    inside one pale-blue band (DESIGN.md's `cobalt-blue-light` token,
    #E6EEFF) instead of three separate white sections — the mockup's
    biggest structural difference from v3.
  - The CTA moved from after the benefits list to inside this band,
    matching the mockup's order.
  - Added a short headline above the existing specific invite sentence — a
    deliberate two-tier copy structure per the mockup, confirmed with the
    user rather than assumed. Uses the mockup's own literal wording,
    "Welcome to the club" (DESIGN.md's `headline` token, 24px/600) — a
    first pass substituted invented copy ("You're invited") here instead
    of the user's actual reference text; corrected on review. Every other
    existing sentence/line is preserved verbatim, just repositioned. The
    headline runs full-width on its own; the distributor's circular mark
    floats beside the specific sentence right below it instead (also
    corrected on review — it was first placed beside the short headline,
    which read as the mark identifying "the club" rather than identifying
    who the specific sentence is about).
  - The benefits list dropped its amber callout box (the pale-blue hero
    band now carries that "highlight" role) for a checklist: a small
    2-cell table per row (icon cell + text cell) rather than a
    hanging-indent div — real-browser verification (not just markup
    review) caught that negative text-indent on a row's containing block
    silently deletes an inline-block child's own text content in this
    rendering engine (the circle painted, the checkmark glyph inside it
    did not); the table approach has no such failure mode and still gets
    wrapped second lines aligned under the label text for free, via the
    text cell's own column width. Small solid-fill circular checkmark
    (Success Green #16A34A, a real DESIGN.md semantic token, white glyph)
    — confirmed with the user as Success Green rather than Cobalt,
    specifically so it doesn't dilute the Confident Blue Rule (Cobalt
    stays reserved for the CTA alone). A unicode glyph rather than a drawn
    icon is a deliberate medium call, not an oversight: HTML email has no
    reliable SVG/icon-font support across clients (Outlook desktop in
    particular), and an <img>-based icon would both add an external asset
    dependency and break the "exactly one <img> when no distributor logo
    is set" invariant this template already holds.
  - The header wordmark grew (36px→40px icon, 18px→20px text) to read as a
    standalone header moment rather than compact chrome, matching the
    mockup's bigger top lockup; the exact tested icon+"stocd"/"up" two-span
    markup is unchanged.
  - Kept, unchanged from v3: hard 0px corners and flat hairline-bordered
    card edges (the mockup's rounded corners/drop shadow are not part of
    this world — DESIGN.md's Square Edge and Reach rules), and the
    float+clearfix technique for the circular distributor mark and its
    mobile shrink.
-->
<mj-head>
  <mj-title>{{distributorName}} invited you to Stocdup</mj-title>
  <mj-font name="Inter" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  <mj-attributes>
    <mj-all font-family="Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" />
    <!-- DESIGN.md's `body` token exactly (14px/400/1.5) — was an invented
         15px/1.6. padding:0 is deliberate: MJML's own mj-text default is
         10px top / 25px sides, which was silently stacking on top of every
         section's own padding. Each mj-text below sets only the
         padding-bottom it needs; section padding is the only other spacing
         source, so the declared card rhythm is actually the one in effect. -->
    <mj-text font-size="14px" font-weight="400" line-height="1.5" color="#0B1D3A" padding="0" />
  </mj-attributes>
  <!-- Shrinks the floated distributor mark on narrow viewports — at the
       full 60px it was wrapping the headline into cramped lines on a
       375px phone. Non-inline (only clients that honor <style>/media
       queries apply it; others keep the 60px desktop size, a safe,
       non-breaking fallback, not a functional regression). -->
  <mj-style>
    @media only screen and (max-width:480px) {
      .distributor-byline-logo {
        width: 44px !important;
        height: 44px !important;
        border-radius: 23px !important;
        margin: 0 12px 6px 0 !important;
      }
    }
  </mj-style>
</mj-head>
<mj-body background-color="#F2F4F7" width="480px">

  <!-- Header: icon-only mark + real live text, not a wordmark baked into an
       image — mirrors the admin app's own chrome lockup exactly
       (apps/admin/src/components/Sidebar.tsx), sized up from that chrome's
       36px/18px so this reads as a standalone header moment (matching the
       v4 mockup's bigger top lockup) rather than compact in-app chrome.
       Padding is symmetric (32px top/bottom) so the lockup sits centered in
       its own white zone before the hero band's color starts — an earlier
       pass left the section's bottom padding at 0, which read as lopsided
       (32px of air above the logo, none below it). -->
  <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="32px 32px 32px" border="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-bottom="none">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-text align="center" padding-bottom="0">
        <img src="{{stocdupIconUrl}}" alt="" width="40" height="40" style="width:40px;height:40px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:12px;" /><span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1;vertical-align:middle;"><span style="color:#0B1D3A;">stocd</span><span style="color:#1565FF;">up</span></span>
      </mj-text>
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

  <!-- Hero band: identity mark, headline, detail copy and the CTA all live
       together on one pale-blue tint (DESIGN.md's cobalt-blue-light token)
       instead of separate white sections — the v4 mockup's central
       structural idea. Headline text is the mockup's own literal copy,
       "Welcome to the club" — not invented wording; DESIGN.md's Headline
       scale (24px/600) is used for it. It runs full-width, on its own,
       NOT wrapped around the distributor's circular mark: the mark floats
       inside the SAME text block as the specific, factual sentence right
       below it ("{{distributorName}} has invited you to access its online
       catalogue…", unchanged copy from v3) so the mark reads as identifying
       who that sentence is about, exactly like an author photo beside a
       byline — a trailing clear:both div is the clearfix, so the column's
       height still accounts for the image even if the sentence is shorter
       than it is tall. Graceful degradation: with no uploaded logo, the
       image tag is simply absent and the sentence runs full-width. -->
  <mj-section background-color="#E6EEFF" padding="32px 32px 0" border-left="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-right="1px solid #E6ECF2">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-text font-size="24px" font-weight="600" line-height="1.3" color="#0B1D3A" padding-bottom="16px">
        Welcome to the club
      </mj-text>
      <mj-text color="#0B1D3A" padding-bottom="8px">
        {{#if distributorLogoUrl}}<img src="{{distributorLogoUrl}}" alt="{{distributorName}}" width="60" height="60" class="distributor-byline-logo" style="float:left;width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:31px;border:1px solid #E6ECF2;margin:0 16px 8px 0;" />{{/if}}<strong>{{distributorName}}</strong> has invited you to access its online catalogue and place orders through <strong>Stocdup</strong>.<div style="clear:both;"></div>
      </mj-text>
      <mj-text color="#5B6B7F" padding-bottom="24px">
        Your account will be connected to <strong style="color:#0B1D3A;">{{customerName}}</strong>, giving you access to the products, prices and delivery options available to your business.
      </mj-text>
      <mj-button href="{{inviteUrl}}" background-color="#1565FF" color="#FFFFFF" font-size="15px"
        font-weight="600" border-radius="0" padding="0 0 32px" inner-padding="14px 32px" align="center">
        Accept invitation
      </mj-button>
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

  <!-- Benefits checklist: the amber callout box from v3 is gone — the hero
       band above now carries that "highlight" role — replaced with a
       checklist read. Each row is a small 2-cell table (icon cell + text
       cell) rather than v3's hanging-indent div: empirically verified (real
       Chromium render, not just markup review) that negative text-indent on
       the row's containing block makes an inline-block child's own text
       content (the checkmark glyph) disappear in this engine — the circle
       itself still painted, but the glyph inside it vanished — while the
       table approach doesn't have that failure mode and still gets wrapped
       second lines aligned under the label text (via the text cell's own
       column width) for free. Success Green (#16A34A, a real DESIGN.md
       semantic token) fill, white glyph. Row spacing widened to DESIGN.md's
       `lg` (20px) token, matching the mockup's roomier list. -->
  <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="24px 32px 0" border-left="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-right="1px solid #E6ECF2">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-text padding-bottom="16px" font-weight="600" font-size="14px">
        Through Stocdup, you can:
      </mj-text>
      <mj-text padding-bottom="20px">
        <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;"><tr>
          <td width="20" valign="top" style="width:20px;padding-right:10px;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:10px;background-color:#16A34A;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;line-height:20px;text-align:center;">&#10003;</span></td>
          <td valign="top" style="font-size:14px;color:#0B1D3A;line-height:1.5;">Browse {{distributorName}}'s catalogue</td>
        </tr></table>
      </mj-text>
      <mj-text padding-bottom="20px">
        <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;"><tr>
          <td width="20" valign="top" style="width:20px;padding-right:10px;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:10px;background-color:#16A34A;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;line-height:20px;text-align:center;">&#10003;</span></td>
          <td valign="top" style="font-size:14px;color:#0B1D3A;line-height:1.5;">See your agreed products and prices</td>
        </tr></table>
      </mj-text>
      <mj-text padding-bottom="20px">
        <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;"><tr>
          <td width="20" valign="top" style="width:20px;padding-right:10px;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:10px;background-color:#16A34A;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;line-height:20px;text-align:center;">&#10003;</span></td>
          <td valign="top" style="font-size:14px;color:#0B1D3A;line-height:1.5;">Choose an available delivery date</td>
        </tr></table>
      </mj-text>
      <mj-text padding-bottom="0">
        <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;"><tr>
          <td width="20" valign="top" style="width:20px;padding-right:10px;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:10px;background-color:#16A34A;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;line-height:20px;text-align:center;">&#10003;</span></td>
          <td valign="top" style="font-size:14px;color:#0B1D3A;line-height:1.5;">Place and review orders online</td>
        </tr></table>
      </mj-text>
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

  <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="24px 32px 0" border-left="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-right="1px solid #E6ECF2">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="0.02em" color="#5B6B7F" padding-bottom="0">
        This invitation was sent to {{recipientEmail}} and will expire on {{expiresAtFormatted}}.
      </mj-text>
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

  <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="24px 32px 32px" border-left="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-right="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-bottom="1px solid #E6ECF2">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-color="#E6ECF2" padding-top="0" padding-bottom="16px" />
      {{#if distributorContactLine}}
      <mj-text font-size="12px" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="0.02em" color="#5B6B7F" padding-bottom="8px">
        Questions about your account, products or pricing? Contact {{distributorName}} at {{distributorContactLine}}.
      </mj-text>
      {{/if}}
      <mj-text font-size="12px" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="0.02em" color="#5B6B7F" padding-bottom="0">
        Need help using Stocdup? Contact {{stocdupSupportEmail}}.
      </mj-text>
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

  <!-- Footer, outside the card -->
  <mj-section padding="24px 32px 0">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="0.02em" color="#5B6B7F">
        Stocdup provides the online ordering service used by {{distributorName}}.
      </mj-text>
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

</mj-body>
</mjml>
